      "artist": "Mike McBey",
      "description": "Pikes Peak is a 14,115 ft (4302m) mountain 12 miles (19 km) west of downtown Colorado Springs, Colorado.\nDespite its height it's not difficult to get to the top. You can drive to the top or (as I did) use the Pikes Peak Cog Railway and enjoy the view all the way up. It's a great journey. \nEn route, you pass the part known as Windy Point, which at 12,129 ft (3697 m) is above the tree line and exposed to the elements - hence the name. This is a passing place for the trains on what is otherwise a single track railroad.\n\nIn the picture we see the old station which is no longer in use and appears to be a home/shelter for Marmots now. I also saw Bighorn Sheep somehow eking out a life near this inhospitable, barren spot.",
